From cb924b52fd6b68d84b97e0a5fa6ec081bb14d136 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:43:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): defer placement of cards with parents to the
 routed gateway [daveey]

A card with parents stayed on the creating gateway because dependencies are local
links, so every orchestrator fan-out child (parents=[self]) and every follow-up of a
MacBook card ran on the MacBook (15 of 175 cards created in 24 h stayed local only for
that reason). decide() now applies every other rule first and answers defer=<target>
for such a card; kanban_create records a placement_deferred event. When its parents
finish, the dispatcher spawns hermes_cli.kanban_placement_forward instead of a worker:
it creates the card on the target through hermes-hub (parent handoffs in the body,
same origin chat), parks the local card on a wait-check probe of the remote card, and
completes it when the remote card is done, so local grandchildren still wait for the
real work. Not live / refused / error before the target accepted it -> the deferral is
cancelled and the forwarder execs the normal worker. kanban.placement.defer_parents
(default true) turns it off.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_db_dispatch.py          |   8 +
 hermes_cli/kanban_placement.py            |  20 +-
 hermes_cli/kanban_placement_forward.py    | 292 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_placement.py | 270 +++++++++++++++++++-
 tools/kanban_tools.py                     |  16 +-
 5 files changed, 601 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 hermes_cli/kanban_placement_forward.py

